# UX-SPEC.md §3.12 C and [D-17] — a fleetd that stalls rather than dies comes back *reconnected*,
# not *restarted*, and the banner must not claim the terminals died.
#
# `daemon stop` is SIGSTOP: the process keeps its PID lock, so nothing restarts it and nothing
# takes its socket — it simply stops answering the health probe, which is the stalled daemon of
# §3.12 C. `daemon cont` lets it answer again. Because the same process comes back with the same
# pid and boot id, the app must report `restarted == false`; that is the difference between the
# 800 ms "reconnected" banner and the 6 s sentence that says the sessions are gone.
#
# Headless: the `shot` fails in the headless lane ("no pixels"), so the file as written is
# virtual-only — but nothing else in it touches the keyboard, so this is the first scenario the
# headless subset can adopt once a shot-free variant is wanted there.
fixture: one-repo
await idle 20000
assert daemon.link == connected

daemon stop
await daemon.link == lost 45000
shot stalled

daemon cont
await daemon.link == reconnected 60000
assert daemon.restarted == false
dump reconnected

# The 800 ms dwell is the app's own, so `advance` retires it without a wall-clock sleep.
advance 1000
await daemon.link == connected 5000
quit
